; `sizeof` and `alignof` take a TYPE, like `cast`'s first argument.
; The operand used to be ignored - `(alignof 00)` checked clean and
; answered 8, while `fmt` refused it (the seeded fuzzer's m00120) -
; so a literal operand is AX3002 now. The help names the form that
; was written, not `cast`'s.
(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (+ (sizeof 99) (alignof 00)))
